# Mutation cases for the `<content expr>` of an `<invoke>` a host runs, in a
# `datamodel="sce-static"` machine generated as C11
# (docs/SCE_ACCEPTED_SUBSET.md §2.15).
#
# Run with
# `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/a_static_c_host_invoke_content_expr_is_the_body_it_is_handed_ctest.cases`.
#
# The expression is C the lowering wrote, a string read from the machine's own
# fields when the invocation starts, and the template only places it: the string
# is the `content` the host is handed, the body the service runs. One that cannot
# be computed — a checked multiplication that overflows — is an attribute that
# cannot be evaluated (W3C SCXML 6.4.1): `error.execution` is raised and nothing
# starts, so the host is never asked.
#
# What is easy to get wrong and reads as success: a body that is never read is a
# request that still looks complete, and a body that failed but started the
# invocation anyway hands the service nothing to run. `statechart_static_host_params`
# tells them apart: its body is `label`, read through a condition over `huge`, and
# `bloat` makes only that condition fail while the `src` still computes.
#
# The generated machine is built from the template at build time, so the template
# is the declared target and the build is what carries a mutation into it.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_ctest --test-dir build -R '^c11_integration_static_host_params$'
mutation_targets tools/codegen/templates/c/invoke_methods.jinja2
mutation_oracles backends/c/tests/integration/test_static_host_params.c sce-build/tests/fixtures/host_processor/statechart_static_host_params.scxml

# ── The body is read and handed over ───────────────────────────────

mutation_case "a body that was computed is not the content the host is handed" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/c/invoke_methods.jinja2",
     "{% if invoke_info.native_content %}_host_inv_content_native{% elif",
     "{% if invoke_info.native_content %}\"\"{% elif")
PY

# ── A body that cannot be computed starts nothing ──────────────────

mutation_case "an invoke whose body failed starts all the same" <<'PY'
edit("tools/codegen/templates/c/invoke_methods.jinja2",
     "\"<invoke> content expr failed to evaluate\");\n{% endif %}\n                    continue;\n",
     "\"<invoke> content expr failed to evaluate\");\n{% endif %}\n")
PY
